  "setup": "One Intel Arc Pro B70 (32 GB, Xe2), render node passthrough only (--device /dev/dri/renderDN); the entrypoint links /dev/dri/by-path for oneCCL. Allocates 268,201 fp8 KV tokens at 262,144 context with vision and DSpark spec decoding (mem 0.815, SWA ratio 0.03, chunk 4096); scheduler VRAM ~30.4 GiB, so leave the card otherwise idle (a desktop session on the same card can push it into xe job timeouts). First start JIT-compiles the Triton kernels (~3 min to ready); the SYCL kernels are prebuilt in the image. Decode with DSpark at 8k context, temp 0.7: ~98 tok/s on code (accept ~4.4), ~47 tok/s on prose (accept ~2.1).",
